  "solution": {
    "text": "Isoelectronic species are known as atoms or ions that have the same number of electrons.<table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"1\" cellspacing=\"1\" style=\"width: 500px;\">\t<tbody>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\">Species</td>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Al</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math></td>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Mg</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math></td>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Be</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math></td>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup></math></td>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Br</mi><mo>-</mo></msup></math></td>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Cl</mi><mo>-</mo></msup></math></td>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Li</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></math></td>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup></math></td>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></math></td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\">No. of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mo>-</mo></msup></math></td>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn></math></td>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn></math></td>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math></td>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn></math></td>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>36</mn></math></td>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>18</mn></math></td>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math></td>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>18</mn></math></td>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>18</mn></math></td>\t\t</tr>\t</tbody></table><p>So <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Mg</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup></math> are isoelectronic with&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Al</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math></p>",
